                            No message is composed for them and none is skipped silently &mdash; add the group above,
                            then run this again
                        </p>
                        <div class="table-scroll" id="lo-unmapped-wrap"></div>
                        <p class="note" id="lo-unmapped-summary"></p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">
                    Overdue orders
                    <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("lo-orders-wrap", "Overdue orders", "Late Orders")' />
                </div>
                <div class="card accent-red">
                    <h3>Every order past its deadline and still unshipped</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        The exported deadline and the offset deadline sit side by side so the offset's effect is
                        visible on every row rather than taken on trust
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-scroll" id="lo-orders-wrap"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">
                    Where the rows went
                    <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("lo-funnel-wrap", "Funnel", "Late Orders")' />
                </div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Every row in the file, accounted for</h3>
                    <p class="sub">The first six buckets are terminal and add up to the row count</p>
                    <div class="table-scroll is-full" id="lo-funnel-wrap"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">
                    Set aside for review
                    <partial name="_ExportButton" model='new ExportButton("lo-review-wrap", "Set aside", "Late Orders")' />
                </div>
                <div class="card accent-amber">
                    <h3>Unshipped rows that were not turned into a warning</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        An unfamiliar status or an unreadable deadline lands here instead of defaulting into
                        &ldquo;chase the seller&rdquo;
                    </p>
                    <div class="table-scroll" id="lo-review-wrap"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">Message wording</div>
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>What each seller is sent</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        Two templates: the envelope is rendered once per seller, the order line once per overdue
                        order. Edits are saved with the mapping above
                    </p>

                    <div class="field">
                        <label for="lo-template">Message</label>
                        <textarea id="lo-template" rows="10" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
                    </div>
                    <div class="field" style="margin-top: 14px">
                        <label for="lo-line-template">Order line</label>
                        <textarea id="lo-line-template" rows="2" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
                    </div>

                    <p class="note">Placeholders: <span id="lo-placeholders"></span></p>

                    <div class="actions">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="lo-render">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Re-render messages</span>
                        </button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-template-reset">
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Reset to default</span>
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="section-title">Messages</div>
                <div class="card accent-green">
                    <h3>One message per seller, exactly as it will be sent</h3>
                    <p class="sub">
                        Read the group name on each card before you copy it &mdash; that is the last chance to catch
                        a wrong mapping
                    </p>

                    <div id="lo-messages"></div>

                    <div class="actions">
                        <label class="check" for="lo-dry-run">
                            <input type="checkbox" id="lo-dry-run" checked />
                            <span>Dry run (compose and verify, but do not send)</span>
                        </label>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="lo-send" disabled>
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Send messages</span>
                        </button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" id="lo-messages-export" disabled>
                            <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="btn-text">Download messages (Excel)</span>
                        </button>
                        <span class="filter-summary" id="lo-messages-summary"></span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="alert" id="lo-messages-alert" role="alert">
                        <strong>Check this</strong>
                        <span class="msg"></span>
                    </div>

                    <p class="note">
                        A dry run opens every group, checks the title matches, types the message and reads it back
                        &mdash; then clears the box without sending. It exercises the whole path against real
                        production data with no outward effect, and it is the routine to run before every live send.
                        You can also still copy a message by hand from its card.
                    </p>
                </div>
